{"id": "24235", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=24235", "title": "New Canaan (Connecticut)", "text": "New Canaan is a town in Connecticut. The town is one of the most affluent communities in the United States. In 2008, CNN Money ranked New Canaan first in the nation with the highest median family income.\nGet in.\nBy train.\nNew Canaan has two Metro-North railroad stations: and, both on the New Canaan Branch of the New Haven Line. \nTravel time to Grand Central Terminal in New York City is approximately one hour."}
{"id": "24236", "revid": "235382", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=24236", "title": "New Carlisle", "text": "New Carlisle is a city in Clark County, Ohio.\nUnderstand.\nNew Carlisle was established in 1810 and certified as an Ohio city in 1973. The downtown area is a historic area, and was built back in 1810.\nGet in.\nBy plane.\nNew Carlisle is about a 20-minute drive from Dayton Airport.\nGet around.\nThe downtown area is best navigated on foot. As there are no hotels in central New Carlisle, a car is recommended to get to a hotel. There are no buses."}
